evealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the exact discriminator for 'fsck could not run' vs 'completed with findings' in the plan body (since an uninitialised store exits 1, not 2), rather than deferring it to an external oracle comment.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.13,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'an uninitialised store also exits 1, not 2 — see the \"Second defect found by the held-out oracle\" comment for the exact discriminator used instead'","AC2: 'A genuine execution failure (fsck could not run, rc not in 0|1) remains distinguishable'","Step 1: 'Raises RebarError when fsck could not RUN'"],"finding":"AC2 states the execution-failure discriminator as 'rc not in 0|1', but the Mechanism note reports an uninitialised store also exits 1, and defers the actual discriminator used to an external 'Second defect found by the held-out oracle' comment not reproduced in the plan. The plan text does not state how a could-not-run store is distinguished from a completed-with-findings run.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f62673273a605bc17","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Mechanism note ('NOTE (corrected during implementation)...') and AC2","norm_id":"n51e4608ea4c9c775","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor implementing fsck_report must decide how to detect could-not-run but rc==1 (uninitialised store) — the rule is only in an external comment, not the plan."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Inline the discriminator into Step 1 / AC2 (e.g. 'treat rc==1 with an uninitialised-store marker in the JSON as could-not-run; rc in {0,1} otherwise = completed run; any other rc = execution failure').","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["vague/subjective terms present: sufficient"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py to the patch-site inventory: move `fsck` out of EXEMPT_GENERIC and into CANONICAL mapped to schemas.FSCK (and delete the now-false 'returns a human summary string' reason), since the tool will begin advertising an outputSchema.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.625,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 4: 'src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py — fsck returns FsckOut ... so the tool advertises an outputSchema like every read tool registered around it.'","Plan step 5 registers only 'FsckOut -> fsck in check_mcp_models.MODEL_SCHEMAS'; it does not name the output-schema-coverage test.","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py:100-101 EXEMPT_GENERIC['fsck'] = 'MCP fsck returns a human summary string; the canonical fsck schema describes the CLI/library --output json shape, not the MCP string' — a string-keyed classification, not a structural reference.","Same file lines 43-77 CANONICAL maps schema-advertising tools to their canonical schema (e.g. bridge_fsck -> schemas.BRIDGE_FSCK); fsck now needs an entry here mapping to schemas.FSCK."],"finding":"The MCP `fsck` tool is changed to advertise an outputSchema (FsckOut / schemas.FSCK), but the plan's affected-file/patch-site inventory omits tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py, which classifies `fsck` as a string-ack exemption in EXEMPT_GENERIC (a string dict-key reference the LSP does not surface). Once fsck advertises a schema, that entry is semantically wrong: fsck now returns a structured result and belongs in CANONICAL (validated against schemas.FSCK), and its recorded reason ('MCP fsck returns a human summary string ... not the MCP string') is false.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f723a2d1b21d1869b","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan steps 4-5 ('fsck returns FsckOut ... advertises an outputSchema'; register FsckOut -> fsck in MODEL_SCHEMAS) and the Test plan — no mention of test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py","norm_id":"nf51f55adf3515901","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py: fsck stays in EXEMPT_GENERIC with a now-false reason, so the newly-structured fsck result is never validated against schemas.FSCK on a real fixture store — a canonical-shape regression the test was built to catch silently escapes.","The same file's CANONICAL dict never gains a 'fsck': schemas.FSCK entry, so the plan under-delivers the 'advertises an outputSchema like every read tool' claim by leaving the tool unvalidated."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py, remove the `fsck` key from EXEMPT_GENERIC and add `\"fsck\": schemas.FSCK` to the CANONICAL dict so the new structured result is validated against its canonical schema; sweep for other string-keyed references to the MCP `fsck` tool name (e.g. in check_mcp_models and schema-coverage tests) that the LSP will not surface.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Give the recover=True path its own representation (e.g. a `mode` discriminator with the narrative returned verbatim and issues[] left empty) instead of running its plain-English output through the scan-oriented `_transform_json`, because that regex fabricates {kind:'warn'} findings from narrative WARN: lines and recover's exit codes (1=completed recovery) do not share fsck's 0/1 vocabulary.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["fsck_recover.py:1-12 documents recover as narrative output with exit vocabulary 0=nothing/recovered, 1=attempted-but-nothing-recovered, 2=fatal, 3=stale — NOT the fsck 0/1 clean/issues vocabulary","fsck_recover.py:250,255 emit literal 'WARN: rebase --continue ...' narrative lines","_transform_json (fsck.py:110-146) matches `^([A-Z_]+):\\s*(.*)$` and would turn those WARN prose lines into {kind:'warn'} issues[] entries, discarding the rest of the narrative","A uniform scan-shaped payload cannot faithfully represent recover's actions-not-findings output; recover needs its own representation (mode discriminator / separate reader)"],"finding":"Step 1's mechanism for the recover=True path — routing fsck_recover_cli's output through the shared _transform_json — is unsound: the recover path emits plain-English narrative (no KIND: lines) with a different exit-code vocabulary, and _transform_json's `^([A-Z_]+):` regex will fabricate {kind:'warn'} findings from the narrative's literal 'WARN: rebase --continue failed' lines while discarding the narrative entirely.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0a9bf89a9cd468b8","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 ('The recover=True path has no --output json in fsck_recover_cli, so its text is put through the SAME shared _transform_json transform for a uniform shape.')","norm_id":"n3d4f7fd2059b1fd7","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["MCP fsck(recover=True) on a store with a paused rebase whose narrative contains a WARN: line — caller sees invented findings and no recovery narrative","recover exit 1 (attempted-but-nothing-recovered, a COMPLETED recovery) collides with fsck's exit-1=issues meaning"],"severity":"none",